        "newsData": {
          "0": {
            "id": "14021564",
            "headline": "Deepa Jewellers IPO: Issue subscribed 5x so far on last day of bidding; check latest GMP",
            "heading": "Deepa Jewellers IPO: Issue subscribed 5x so far on last day of bidding; check latest GMP",
            "intro": "The initial public offering (IPO) of the Telangana-based hallmarked gold jewellery supplier, Deepa Jewellers, continued its impressive demand on the final day of bidding, with the issue receiving 4.70 times subscription as of 10:35 am on September 3, as per the NSE data.",
            "body": "The initial public offering (IPO) of the Telangana-based hallmarked gold jewellery supplier, Deepa Jewellers, continued its impressive demand on the final day of bidding, with the issue receiving 5.01 times subscription as of 10:35 am on September 3, as per the NSE data.\r\n\r\nThe IPO received bids for 9,27,11,808 equity shares against 1,85,20,085 shares on offer, with retail investors accounting for 6.01 times subscription of their reserved portion. The non-institutional investor (NII) category was subscribed 8.5 times during the period.\r\n\r\nThe Telangana-based company, which supplies hallmarked gold jewellery to retail chains and standalone stores, has fixed the IPO price band at Rs 168-177 per share. The issue will remain open until September 3.\r\n\r\nRead Also:\u00a0Rays of Belief IPO booked over 5x so far on Day 3; GMP at 20%\r\n\r\nIn the grey market, Deepa Jewellers shares were commanding a premium of Rs 28 on September 3, according to InvestorGain. At the upper end of the IPO price band of Rs 177, the GMP implies an indicative listing price of Rs 205, translating into a potential listing gain of 15.82 percent.\r\n\r\nInvestors must note that the grey market premium is an unofficial indicator and can change before the shares are listed.\r\n\r\nAhead of the public issue, Deepa Jewellers raised Rs 137.91 crore from 14 anchor investors. The company allotted 77.91 lakh shares to the anchor investors at the upper end of the price band.\r\n\r\nThe anchor book included investors such as Nomura Singapore, Ashoka India Equity Investment Trust Plc and Citigroup. Of the total anchor allocation, 14.96 lakh shares were allotted to domestic mutual funds, including Tata Asset Management Company and Unifi Mutual Fund.\r\n\r\nMotilal Oswal Finvest was the largest investor in the anchor book, picking up 20.3 lakh shares worth Rs 35.95 crore. WhiteOak Capital and 360 ONE each acquired 5.08 lakh shares, with each investment amounting to nearly Rs 9 crore.\r\n\r\nThe company is looking to raise up to Rs 459.72 crore through the IPO, comprising a fresh issue of Rs 250 crore and an offer for sale (OFS) of up to 1.18 crore equity shares by promoter Ashish Agarwal and his wife Seema.\r\n\r\nCheck IPO News Here\r\n\r\nDeepa Jewellers plans to deploy Rs 215 crore from the net proceeds of the fresh issue towards long-term working capital requirements, including procurement, maintenance and scaling up of inventory. The remaining proceeds will be used for general corporate purposes.\r\n\r\nThe IPO has a lot size of 84 shares, requiring a minimum investment of Rs 14,868 for retail investors at the upper price band. The shares are scheduled to list on the BSE and NSE on September 8, subject to the IPO timeline.\r\n\r\nEmkay Global Financial Services and Valmiki Leela Capital are the book-running lead managers to the issue.\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: The views and investment tips expressed by investment experts on Moneycontrol.com are their own and not those of the website or its management. Moneycontrol.com advises users to check with certified experts before taking any investment decisions.",
