          "1": {
            "id": "14021531",
            "headline": "Arcil fixes IPO price band at Rs 132-139 per share; Rs 733-crore issue to open for subscription on September 9",
            "heading": "Arcil fixes IPO price band at Rs 132-139 per share; Rs 733-crore issue to open for subscription on September 9",
            "intro": "The IPO will make Arcil the first asset reconstruction company to tap the primary market for fundraising through a public issue. The offer, comprising entirely an offer for sale (OFS) of 5.27 crore equity shares, will open on September 9 and close on September 11.",
            "body": "Asset Reconstruction Company (India) on September 3 fixed the price band at Rs 132-139 per share for its upcoming Rs 732.9-crore initial public offering (IPO), valuing the company at Rs 4,516 crore.\r\n\r\nThe IPO will make Arcil the first asset reconstruction company to tap the primary market for fundraising through a public issue. The offer, comprising entirely an offer for sale (OFS) of 5.27 crore equity shares, will open on September 9 and close on September 11.\r\n\r\nAll the net IPO proceeds will accrue to the selling shareholders \u2014 New York-headquartered global investment firm Avenue Capital Group-owned Avenue India Resurgence, State Bank of India, Lathe Investment and Federal Bank. Arcil will not receive any proceeds from the offer.\r\n\r\nPromoters Avenue India Resurgence and State Bank of India own 69.73 percent and 19.95 percent stakes in Arcil, respectively, while Singapore sovereign wealth fund GIC-backed Lathe Investment holds a 5 percent stake in the company.\r\n\r\nThe one-day anchor book will open for institutional investors on September 8, while the IPO share allotment is likely to be finalised by September 15. Trading in Arcil shares is expected to commence on the stock exchanges on September 17.\r\n\r\nInvestors can bid for a minimum of 107 equity shares, with subsequent bids to be made in multiples of 107 shares. Accordingly, the minimum investment for retail investors would be Rs 14,873, while the maximum investment would be Rs 1,93,349.\r\n\r\nClick Here To Read All IPO News\r\n\r\nHalf of the offer size has been reserved for qualified institutional buyers (QIBs), while 35 percent has been allocated to retail investors and the remaining 15 percent to non-institutional investors (NIIs).\r\n\r\nAs an asset reconstruction company (ARC), Arcil acquires stressed assets from banks and financial institutions and implements resolution strategies through restructuring, enforcement of rights over underlying securities and settlements. The company aims to maximise recoveries and optimise the value of stressed assets to generate revenue streams.\r\n\r\nOn the financial front, Arcil reported a 6.7 percent year-on-year increase in profit to Rs 351.7 crore for the fiscal year ended March 2026. Revenue rose 24 percent to Rs 721.7 crore from Rs 581.8 crore during the same period.\r\n\r\nIIFL Capital Services, IDBI Capital Markets &amp;amp; Securities and JM Financial are acting as the merchant bankers for the Asset Reconstruction Company (India) IPO.",
            "posturl": "news/business/ipo/arcil-fixes-price-band-at-rs-132-139-per-share-rs-733-crore-ipo-to-open-for-subscription-on-september-9-14021531.html",
