          "2": {
            "id": "14021548",
            "headline": "Rays of Belief IPO booked over 5x so far on Day 3; GMP at 20%",
            "heading": "Rays of Belief IPO booked over 5x so far on Day 3; GMP at 20%",
            "intro": "The initial public offering (IPO) of Rays of Belief, the parent company of Mom's Belief, remained in strong demand on the last day of bidding, with the issue recording 5.09 times subscription, as of 10:20 am on September 3, as per the NSE data.",
            "body": "The initial public offering (IPO) of Rays of Belief, the parent company of Mom's Belief, remained in strong demand on the last day of bidding, with the issue recording\u00a05.09 times subscription, as of 10:20 am on September 3, as per the NSE data.\r\n\r\nThe Rs 125-crore IPO received bids for 1,59,66,364 equity shares against 31,37,810 shares on offer. Retail investors led the subscription, with their reserved portion subscribed 23.21 times. The non-institutional investor (NII) portion was subscribed 4.86\u00a0times.\r\n\r\nIn the grey market, Rays of Belief shares were commanding a premium of Rs 47 on the morning of September 3, according to InvestorGain. Based on the upper price band of Rs 239, the grey market premium (GMP) indicates a potential listing gain of around 20 percent.\r\n\r\nRead Also:\u00a0Purple Style Labs IPO allotment today; check status on BSE, NSE and registrar\r\n\r\nHowever, GMP is an unofficial indicator based on transactions in the unregulated grey market. The premium can change before listing and does not guarantee the actual listing price or returns.\r\n\r\nAhead of the IPO opening, Rays of Belief raised Rs 50 crore from five institutional investors through its anchor book. The anchor investors were allotted 20.92 lakh shares.\r\n\r\nViney Growth Fund and LRSD Securities were each allotted 6.27 lakh shares worth Rs 15 crore. Nova Global Opportunities Fund acquired 4.18 lakh shares worth Rs 10 crore.\r\n\r\nMeanwhile, 31 Degrees North Fund and Visionary Value Fund were each allotted 2.09 lakh shares worth Rs 5 crore.\r\n\r\nThe company is looking to raise up to Rs 125 crore through the IPO, comprising 52.3 lakh shares. The price band has been fixed at Rs 227-239 per share, with the issue available for subscription from September 1 to September 3.\r\n\r\nThe IPO consists entirely of a fresh issue, with no offer-for-sale component.\r\n\r\nRays of Belief is promoted by Nitin Bindlish through Carving Futures. The company plans to deploy Rs 41.3 crore of the net IPO proceeds towards setting up new centres on leased premises and associated technology hardware costs.\r\n\r\nCheck IPO News Here\r\n\r\nAnother Rs 14.4 crore has been earmarked for lease payments for its existing centres in India, while Rs 10.1 crore will be invested in its subsidiary, Mom\u2019s Belief US Inc, towards lease or licence payments for existing centres in the US.\r\n\r\nThe company will also use Rs 10.2 crore for brand awareness and inclusive outreach programmes. The remaining proceeds will be used to fund inorganic growth through unidentified acquisitions and for general corporate purposes.\r\n\r\nMefcom Capital Markets is the merchant banker for the IPO.\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: The views and investment tips expressed by investment experts on Moneycontrol.com are their own and not those of the website or its management. Moneycontrol.com advises users to check with certified experts before taking any investment decisions.",
